 :change
 {:sut
  "M2's first step: the SUT transacts. One atom holds the db value; POST /ldbc/update swaps it with eng/transact (single writer); every read takes the value it finds (a snapshot per read, no lock on the read path). INS2 (a person likes a post: the reified like, 3 datoms) and INS8 (a friendship: knows both ways + the reified date both ways, 8 datoms) are served; every other insert is a 400, never a 200.",
  :driver
  "--updates <LDBC update stream>: INS2/INS8 parameters in stream order, put in the round-robin mix at the same rate as the reads (the certified driver interleaves by simulation time -- stated). After every sweep, read-after-write: the last 20 inserts of each run must be visible to the read that covers them (INS8 -> IS3 lists the new friend; INS2 -> IC07 on the post's creator lists the liker); an acknowledged insert that is not visible refuses the run.",
  :unverifiable
  "an INS2 on a post this subset does not hold (no creator to read IC07 for) or an INS8 to a person INS1 never created here (no name for IS3 to show) is counted as unverifiable, printed, and not counted as visible. First runs refused on exactly these until the SUT reported them (:creator nil, :p2-known false); :p2-known is 'has a person/firstName', not 'has any datom' -- an earlier INS8 asserts knows datoms onto persons that never existed here."},
 :reading
 ["Two of the eight LDBC inserts are served and interleaved with the eleven reads; the write costs the same as a point read served (1.9 ms at 8 slots, 3.5 at 32) and the 13-op mix runs at 1960 / 3791 ops/s -- level with the 11-op read-only mix on simeon (2047 / 4089) on a different host. Every verifiable insert was visible to its covering read on both sweeps."
  "What is not here: INS1/INS3-7 (persons, comment likes, forums, memberships, posts, comments), the simulation-time interleave and dependency tracking, and the ACID suite. The unverifiable count is high (77 / 91 of 120 samples) because the stream's likes mostly land on posts outside the subset and its friendships mostly involve persons INS1 would have created."
  "M2 stands at 2/8 inserts served with read-after-write; M1 at 11/29 reads with the Neo4j reference. Ratio to the audited No.1: 71 at 8 slots, 37 at 32 -- raw."],
